@startuml Implementation_View
title Smart E-Mobility Hub - Development / Implementation View
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 60
package "Presentation" as Presentation {
  [Student Portal] as StudentUI
  [Operator Portal] as OperatorUI
}
component "API handlers\nSession / source authorization" as API
package "Application and domain modules" as Domain {
  [Fleet & Incident\nFleetService / IncidentService\nTelemetryAdapter] as Fleet
  [Vehicle Rental] as Rental
  [Parking & Private EV] as Parking
  [Smart Charging] as Charging
  [Hub & Identity] as Hub
  [What-if Simulation] as Simulation
}
component "Repository + Unit of Work contracts\nVersioned snapshot contract" as Contracts
component "JSON seed / in-memory adapter\nState lock, command/event ledger, audit" as Data
component "Internal health scheduler" as Scheduler
Presentation --> API : role-scoped requests
API --> Domain : route to owning service
API ..> Hub : authentication
Scheduler --> Fleet : freshness / imbalance
Fleet --> Rental : vehicle operations
Fleet --> Parking : capacity / observations
Fleet --> Charging : point status / incidents
Fleet --> Hub : network status
Rental --> Hub : status / alternatives
Parking --> Hub : status / alternatives
Parking --> Charging : charging requests
Charging ..> Parking : parking eligibility
Domain --> Contracts : owner writes / consistent reads
Simulation ..> Contracts : copy snapshot for each run
Contracts --> Data : atomic publication
legend bottom
  Fleet & Incident owns intake; Rental/Parking/Charging own resource transitions.
  Inter-module arrows are in-process contract dependencies, not separate deployments.
  Simulation modifies its copied snapshot only; recommendations do not dispatch live work.
  Exact Fleet contracts are in architecture_baseline.md and 04-fleet-incident.md.
endlegend
@enduml
